ts³11100670418³1version³13³1cache_oldmajor³14³1cache_oldauthor³14³1cache_diff_default_author³11³1revision³15³1text_default³1ip³2205.231.31.86³2ts³21100670418³2version³21³2name³2text_default³2data³2summary³3*³3text³3Ohio vs. Howard, Ohio 2923.12 ruled unconstitutional,
Scanned and OCRer document from ohioccw.org 
http://www.ohioccw.org/downloads-file-11

"Description: This is an unofficial copy of the Seneca Common Pleas Court decision to dismiss a concealed carry charge against a woman who claimed an affirmative defense "at the scene" as was charged. This document was created by scanning and OCR'ing (character recognition) the entire 18 pages. This is NOT the official version, there are some slight mistakes in the document, and we manually edited it to clean up some of the glaringly obvious errors. We are working on obtaining an electronic copy of the legislation to generate a better copy."

Somewhat similar to Hunter's case.  Howard was a passenger in a car stopped for speeding.  The car was searched ("administrative inventory").  A loaded pistol was found under a seat, which she admitted was hers. She kept it for self defense, having been a victim of rape.  Her _sole_ defense in court, if I read this right, was that the Ohio statutes regarding CCW were contrary to the Ohio state constitution.


Klein v. Lewis http://www.firearmslitigation.org/content/body_home.html (click "Ohio Supreme Court Rules that there is No Constitutional Right to Bear Concealed Weapons" to load the pdf)

Ohio v. Feely http://www.sconet.state.oh.us/rod/documents/0/2003/2003-Ohio-4779.doc  see also http://www.chuckkleinauthor.com/Feely.html (site going away 1mar2004)

